## Getting started

```bash
git config core.hooksPath .githooks   # once per clone: scan commits for secrets
scripts/verify.sh                     # lint, types, tests, secret scan
```

## How work flows

Changes go through a gated pipeline. Two steps are approvals that only a person gives.

1. Talk the design through with Claude, then `/rb-design <name>` writes it to
   `docs/architecture/NNN-name.md` as a draft. Or copy `000-template.md` by hand.
2. `/rb-intake`, then `/rb-research`. Revise the design, then set `status: approved`.
3. `/rb-draft-plan`. Review the plan, then set `status: approved`.
4. `/rb-implement`, one milestone at a time, then `/rb-review-diff`.
5. `scripts/verify.sh` and CI.

Lessons worth keeping go to `docs/knowledge/`; see `docs/knowledge/CONTRIBUTING.md`.
